# Base URL of the web app that serves /api/driver/*.
# A phone cannot reach "localhost" — use your computer's LAN IP for local dev,
# or the deployed dev/prod URL.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.5:3000

# Only needed when EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL points at a Vercel PREVIEW deployment —
# Preview is protected by Vercel Deployment Protection (Production is not).
# Get this value from Vercel: Project Settings -> Deployment Protection ->
# Protection Bypass for Automation. Leave unset when targeting Production or a
# local/LAN server.
EXPO_PUBLIC_VERCEL_PROTECTION_BYPASS=

# Android only. react-native-maps renders a blank map on Android without a
# Google Maps key; iOS uses Apple Maps and needs nothing. Expo Go's shared
# debug key covers `npx expo start`, so this is only required once you make a
# real build (EAS or a local prebuild).
#
# Get one from Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials, with
# "Maps SDK for Android" enabled. Restrict it to the Android package
# `in.bsmp.driver` plus your signing certificate's SHA-1 — the key ships inside
# the APK and is extractable, so that restriction is what protects it, not
# secrecy.
#
# For EAS builds set it as an EAS environment variable rather than committing it:
#   eas env:create --name GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY --scope project
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
